 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>KeyEvent</b> is a class in <code>java.awt.event</code> that represents a keyboard action when the user presses, types, or releases a key.</p>\n<h3>Key Points</h3><ul><li>Belongs to <code>java.awt.event</code> and works with <b>KeyListener</b> or <b>KeyAdapter</b>.</li><li><code>getKeyChar()</code> gives the typed character; <code>getKeyCode()</code> gives the key code (such as <code>KeyEvent.VK_ENTER</code>).</li><li><b>keyPressed</b> – any key pushed down. <b>keyTyped</b> – a character key produces a character. <b>keyReleased</b> – key let go.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"note\">Example: the full program is traced above (copy it into the exam).</p>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which method runs first when you push a key?",
  "options": [
   "keyReleased()",
   "keyPressed()",
   "getKeyChar()"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Pizza Time Rocks: Pressed first!"
 }
